'' Overload resolution. The ranking is, strongest first: exact match, then staying in
'' the class, then widening over narrowing, then the nearest WIDTH, then matching
'' SIGNEDNESS, then the signed/unsigned family partner, then rank. Every one of those
'' orderings was forced by a measured row -- the full 1,274-choice differential is
'' tools/gen/check-overload.py, and it is a FITTED model, not fbc's algorithm.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --check tests/types/src/overload.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 22 byte
'' EXPECT-OUT: 23 short
'' EXPECT-OUT: 24 short
'' EXPECT-OUT: 25 short
'' EXPECT-OUT: 26 short
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 ambiguous
